  "docs": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "inline": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Make an array invariant under a permutation group."
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Summary"
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "inline": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Two modes, differing in whether the discarded entries get a vote.\n"
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "\"reynolds-projection\""
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " (the default) averages each orbit:"
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "inline": [
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "R_G(T) = (1 / |G|) * sum_{g in G} g \u00b7 T"
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "inline": [
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "\"canonical-copy\""
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " instead keeps one entry per orbit -- the one at the\nlexicographically smallest index -- and copies it over the rest. Every\nother value in the orbit is discarded rather than mixed in, which is what\nmakes it the right choice when the input is not trusted: nothing a caller\nhid in the redundant positions can reach the result. It is also the\ncheaper of the two, being one copy pass rather than "
              },
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "|G|"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " transposed\nadds, and it never enumerates the group."
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Extended Summary"
      },
